WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.280
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: Who
doesn't love saving money?

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:05.550
Stay tuned to learn the
secrets of cost optimization

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:06.480
with Anthos.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.980
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:14.950
I'm Priyanka, and
welcome to Anthos 101.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:16.810
In the next five
minutes, we're going

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:20.650
to cover five ways to reduce
your costs using Anthos.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:24.250
So let's jump into
the five in five.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.400
Number one,
improving visibility.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.260
Imagine you have
an application that

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:34.480
was built on premises years ago
but has highly variable usage.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.160
How awesome it
would be to move it

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:39.020
to the cloud to take
advantage of auto-scaling,

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:41.410
so you can pay for
resources when you need them

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:43.250
and not all the time?

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.740
On the other hand,
imagine you have

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:46.750
an app that is running
in the cloud and that

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:48.880
has pretty consistent
traffic patterns,

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:51.370
and you happen to have
capacity on premises.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:53.680
Why not move it there and
leverage your existing

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:55.620
investments?

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:58.410
Now, we know that Anthos
provides consistency

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:01.800
and portability across hybrid
and multi-cloud environments,

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.580
which allows you to see all of
the resources you're consuming

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:08.910
and easily balance and
re-balance them across those

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:10.590
environments, which means--

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:13.460
SPEAKER: [INAUDIBLE]

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:17.220
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: Number two,
reducing operational overhead.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.730
Now, imagine your
platform operations team,

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:22.190
which is responsible for
configuring, patching,

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:25.490
and releasing, not to mention
sometimes migration from one

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:27.170
environment to another.

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:30.200
It is a huge overhead
to do all that

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:33.360
across clouds and on premises.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:35.910
With Anthos, you get
a single pane of glass

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:38.490
for management and
configuration of resources,

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:40.440
which improves productivity.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:43.740
Similarly, your security
team that creates, deploys,

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:46.920
and enforces security policies
across your application

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:49.860
development life
cycles, with Anthos,

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.700
you get to consistently apply
security policies across all

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:57.210
your applications,
spanning cloud and on-prem,

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:58.030
which means--

00:01:58.030 --> 00:01:59.470
SPEAKER: [INAUDIBLE]

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:01.470
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: With
the efficiencies gained,

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:03.510
your teams can
focus their energy

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:06.480
on building great applications.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:10.470
Number three, modernizing
monolithic apps.

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:14.490
Every organization has at least
a few monolithic applications

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:17.220
that are costly to
scale and manage.

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:19.560
While Google Cloud
supports common management

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:21.760
of virtual machines
and containers,

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:24.930
I'm sure you're already looking
to the future of breaking down

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:27.630
your monolithic applications
into container-based

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:29.850
micro-services to
scale and manage

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:32.440
your resources efficiently.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:35.290
Using Migrate for Anthos,
you can turn your VMs

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:38.800
into container-based apps
without having to re-architect

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:41.420
or re-platform manually.

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:43.510
This helps you
simplify operations,

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:47.020
such as dynamic scaling, and
integrate with other Anthos

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:50.680
services, like service mesh,
for better resource monitoring.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:53.260
And by containerizing
your app, you're

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:57.170
able to pack more resources on
less infrastructure, leading

00:02:57.170 --> 00:02:57.670
to--

00:02:57.670 --> 00:02:59.780
SPEAKER: [INAUDIBLE]

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:01.720
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
Number four, removing

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:04.530
the need for hypervisor.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:07.470
If you're running Kubernetes
applications on prem,

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:11.200
you may begin to assess the need
for third-party hypervisors.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:15.630
So we announced that later in
2020 you will be able to run

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:18.630
Anthos with no
third-party hypervisors,

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:21.450
further eliminating the
management overhead of yet

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:24.120
another vendor
relationship and reducing--

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:25.840
SPEAKER: Costs.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:28.850
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: Number
five, optimization tools

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:32.030
available in Google
Cloud Marketplace.

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:34.520
If you're already running
Kubernetes and looking

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:37.520
to optimize costs, check out
Google Cloud Marketplace,

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:40.340
which offers solutions
from commercial partners

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:43.610
and open source projects that
take innovative approaches

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:46.040
to monitor and
report on resources

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:48.020
running within your clusters.

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:51.620
These Kubernetes applications
are pre-integrated with Anthos

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:55.200
and deploy quickly, saving you--

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.120
well, saving you
time, which saves--

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.600
SPEAKER: Costs.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:01.440
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
Often, circumstances

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:04.320
beyond our control
force changes in budgets

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:06.870
and send us into a
cost-saving mode.

